{
 "schema": "triattn_pkg_prebuilt/v2",
 "what": "Prebuilt torch C++/CUDA extensions of the CUDA routes, one directory per stack tag (torch<version>-<CPython SOABI>), four per stack: triattn_sm90_ext (cuda), triattn_mw_ext_g3x4 (cuda_c), triattn_m1_ext (cuda_b) -- sm_90a code -- and triattn_sm80_ext (cuda_80) -- sm_80 code. Each <ext>.json beside an <ext>.so is its build record: kernel directory, torch / CUDA / python / nvcc versions, the ptxas that assembled it, the CUTLASS tag where headers are used, the -gencode flags, and the digests so_sha256 / source_sha256 (every file under the directory's csrc/) / module_sha256 plus loadcheck = {test-vector id: sha256/16 of the output bytes on a device of the extension's architecture}. Every binary was built by tools/build_prebuilt.py inside the stack's own image (its nvcc / ptxas; CUTLASS 4.7.1 headers; TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST scoped per extension) from exactly the sources in this package (tools/check_prebuilt.py re-verifies the digests); output bytes are identical across stacks (equal loadcheck digests).",
